1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,753
[MARIELA] <i>Where are you going?</i>
<i>Why are you all dressed up?</i>

2
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,422
<i>To my new job, Ma.</i>

3
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:08,299
<i>Really? Someone hired you?</i>

4
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:09,384
[ABI] <i>Ms. Camille!</i>

5
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,594
<i>I have an idea for Pebblng.</i>

6
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,638
[BILLY] <i>When a couple meets on LoveList</i>

7
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:15,557
<i>and reaches marriage,</i>

8
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>we celebrate it</i>

9
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:20,562
<i>as the ultimate validation</i>
<i>of our platform.</i>

10
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:21,646
<i>LoveFeast.</i>

11
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:25,066
<i>Turning meaningful connections</i>
<i>into lifelong commitments.</i>

12
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,445
<i>Well done, Abi.</i>
<i>I need someone like you here at Pebblng.</i>

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:30,030
[LINDSAY]<i> I really love the concept.</i>

14
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:32,991
<i>But, apparently, it's a replica</i>
<i>of an existing concept.</i>

15
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>I'm here for Camille.</i>

16
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:35,994
<i>Please tell her it's Billy.</i>

17
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,829
<i>- I'm sure she knows me.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

18
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:42,125
[ABI] <i>Thank you, Ms. Camille,</i>
<i>for liking my concept.</i>

19
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,338
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

20
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,631
[CAMILLE] But…

21
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:53,928
I think we need to change
the color scheme.

22
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:58,558
Because it should be
Pebblng's brand colors.

23
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:01,978
You uploaded LoveList's colors.

24
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:03,772
Ms. Billy…

25
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:05,940
Billy!

26
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:10,153
Oh my God, it's been forever!

27
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:12,572
What are you doing here?

28
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:16,034
Camille, we have to talk.

29
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:18,953
But I'll handle this first.

30
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:28,922
You have a lot to explain, Abi.

31
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:36,763
How did you get your hands
on our LoveFeast concept?

32
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:40,350
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

33
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:41,601
[ABI SCOFFS]

34
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,353
Your concept?

35
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,564
How did this become
your concept, Ms. Billy?

36
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:49,442
You should've at least changed the name.

37
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:52,070
Excuse me, but what are you talking about?

38
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:55,115
I'm sorry, Camille,
you're finding out this way.

39
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,324
But really?

40
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,535
LoveFeast?

41
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:02,789
She stole that from LoveList.

42
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:05,083
Ms. Billy, what are you talking about?

43
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:08,128
I didn't steal anything!
That's my concept!

44
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:11,131
Ms. Camille, believe me.
I didn't steal anything.

45
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:14,592
- Stop, Abi.
- Ms. Billy, you stop!

46
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:17,053
Ms. Billy, you are my idol.

47
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:21,558
But don't take what's mine, Ms. Billy.

48
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,269
Make something of your own!

49
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:26,521
If you can't think of anything,
then I'm sorry,

50
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:29,858
but don't steal my concept, Ms. Billy.

51
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:33,278
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

52
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:36,406
[BLOW LANDS]

53
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,868
- Ow, Ms. Billy!
- Liar! Liar! Liar!

54
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,746
Liar! Liar!

55
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:47,417
[BILLY BREATHES SHAKILY]

56
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,588
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

57
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:52,797
Stop lying.

58
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:57,010
How did you get it?

59
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,638
I'm not lying, Ms. Billy.

60
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:05,351
- I didn't take anything from you.
- God, I thought you just had no choice.

61
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:08,396
That's why you had to lie
on your application.

62
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:11,149
But, guess what, Abi?

63
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:16,112
- You really are a liar.
- [CAMILLE] Abi.

64
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:18,656
- Is that true?
- Uh--

65
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:22,118
[BILLY] Camille, be careful with this one.

66
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:27,999
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

67
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:29,417
She's a liar.

68
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:35,048
[ABI INHALES SHAKILY]

69
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:37,133
Ms. Camille, believe me.

70
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:41,179
I don't know what Ms. Billy is saying
because that is my concept!

71
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:42,805
- That's my idea.
- Enough, Abi. Enough.

72
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:45,225
- Enough with the drama!
- Ms. Billy!

73
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:48,269
I get it now! It's clear to me.

74
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:51,689
I now know what kind of person you are.

75
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,235
You made a choice.

76
00:03:57,528 --> 00:04:00,365
You know this could turn
into a legal case, right?

77
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:05,078
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:05,161 --> 00:04:07,288
You played with the wrong person.

79
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,209
You deceived me.

80
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,336
My company.

81
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:19,050
And I will make sure you face
the consequences.

82
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:22,512
Ms. Billy, please don't threaten me.

83
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:24,264
Oh, it's not a threat, Abi.

84
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:29,310
It's a promise.

85
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:36,693
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:04:53,668 --> 00:05:00,425
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

87
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:07,265
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,805
- [VALERIE] <i>He's mine!</i>
- Wow!

89
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,266
- [KEVIN] <i>And I'm hers!</i>
- They're official now!

90
00:05:50,349 --> 00:05:52,560
A skirt? Does it really have
to be a skirt?

91
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:54,937
What straight man wears a skirt?

92
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,191
- [JORDAN CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- Wait, I'll show you something.

93
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:03,988
Here, look. These are men.

94
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,574
Whatever. He's gay.

95
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:09,410
Why are you so affected?

96
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,704
Look at our boss. He doesn't care!

97
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:13,456
Boss.

98
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,083
You're not jealous anymore, are you?

99
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,335
We're done.

100
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,796
You're on your own.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

101
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:24,801
Congrats! One rival officially eliminated!

102
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,512
[JORDAN CHUCKLES]

103
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,098
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

104
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:32,183
[ROBBIE] Oh, we're still closed!

105
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,353
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

106
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:41,776
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:50,368
Abi stole our entire presentation?

108
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:54,080
Yes. I saw the exact same sheets.

109
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:55,331
But how?

110
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:58,960
I don't know, but…

111
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:01,379
I sent the sheets to your email.

112
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,756
Maybe someone got hacked!

113
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,716
O-Or maybe someone leaked it?

114
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,804
Among us? That seems--
That seems impossible.

115
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:12,682
Who did you send the copies to?

116
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:15,143
To the three of you!
I didn't even send it to Valerie!

117
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,104
[TONI GASPS]

118
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:19,564
This is so stressful!

119
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,315
- My gosh!
- [LIGHTER CLICKING]

120
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:28,406
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

121
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,080
Fire alarm.

122
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:44,297
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

123
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,049
HIGH SCHOOL:
BAGONG SILANG HIGH SCHOOL

124
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:50,887
I can do many things.

125
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:53,431
Yeah, we heard.

126
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:57,810
When it comes to work, you can see
that I'm good, I'm smart.

127
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:00,813
- I'm resourceful.
- But your work isn't spotless.

128
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,106
You got caught, bro.

129
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,567
I would do anything for my mother.

130
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,071
I'm sorry. [INHALES]

131
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:11,032
That's why I played with fire.

132
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,202
Sorry.

133
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:19,165
Believe me, I can help you, sir.
I know a lot about POS!

134
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:22,543
I'm a computer expert, aren't I, boss?

135
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,712
Computer hacking.

136
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:26,506
You should just be a bouncer!

137
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,133
You punch pretty well.

138
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,885
Boss, I'll change.

139
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:32,720
I promise.

140
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:36,057
I just really need a job.

141
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:38,976
If you could please give me a chance.

142
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,853
[CALOY BREATHES SHAKILY]

143
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,688
I don't want to go back to my old ways.

144
00:08:44,106 --> 00:08:45,816
I just really need--

145
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:49,028
I just really need medicine for my mother.

146
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:55,326
We may have reached a settlement,

147
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:58,412
but I still don't trust you.

148
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,292
You think I relaxed
after the hearing at the fiscal?

149
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:05,336
I didn't.

150
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:06,921
We did some digging.

151
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,340
And my lawyer discovered

152
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:12,760
that your mother's not sick.

153
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:14,262
She's been gone for a long time.

154
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:17,014
She left when you were still a child.

155
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,599
I-I don't know what you're saying.

156
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:20,268
Okay.

157
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:23,896
I can have you imprisoned again.

158
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,314
I said I don't know!

159
00:09:27,191 --> 00:09:30,152
You have no right
to speak about my family.

160
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,279
You know, Caloy…

161
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,407
I'm also suspicious of your alibi

162
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,576
about LoveList's former employee.

163
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:37,535
No.

164
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:41,414
But one thing's for sure. I'll find out.

165
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,543
And I'll discover who your boss is.

166
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:46,961
[FOLDER THUDS]

167
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,424
I said I don't know
what you're talking about!

168
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:56,887
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,264
[CHAIR SLAMS]

170
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:04,061
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN, CLOSES]

171
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,816
I did apply to their company.

172
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:12,862
But it's not true that
I lied on my application.

173
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,447
To be honest,

174
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:17,241
I noticed a lot of shortcomings
in LoveList.

175
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:20,453
That's why I gave them
a lot of good suggestions.

176
00:10:20,536 --> 00:10:23,664
LoveFeast was one of my suggestions!

177
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:25,124
They were so impressed by it!

178
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,793
That's why I thought
they were going to hire me.

179
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:30,463
But Ms. Billy rejected me.

180
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,841
Classic Billy. She's a thief.

181
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:37,053
We both ran for student council president
back in university.

182
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:39,889
I led the polls in the first two hours.

183
00:10:39,972 --> 00:10:41,932
But she suddenly won!

184
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:45,186
Up to this day, I know it was rigged.

185
00:10:48,147 --> 00:10:49,106
[ABI EXHALES]

186
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:52,151
I also felt that deceit.

187
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:56,822
But, Ms. Camille, I'm here…

188
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,450
[ABI GULPS, SNIFFLES]

189
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,662
…because my mom is sick.

190
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:05,498
I really need a job.

191
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:07,750
I said the same thing to Ms. Billy,

192
00:11:07,833 --> 00:11:09,251
but she didn't care.

193
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:12,588
So I thought about where else to apply.

194
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:13,881
I thought of Pebblng.

195
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,549
That's why I stormed in earlier.

196
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,719
Because I really wanted to
present my idea to you.

197
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,763
Because I really need money.

198
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:23,891
I need a job to pay for
my mother's medical expenses.

199
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,519
Well, her loss is my gain.

200
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:30,606
Morrie, go ahead and orient her.

201
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:33,651
- Oh, orient as in…?
- As in, I am the boss.

202
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:35,486
I can hire instantly. Is there a problem?

203
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:36,862
Of course not.

204
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,280
All right.

205
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:41,409
Thank you so much, Ms. Camille!

206
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:48,374
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:59,301
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

208
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,316
I knew it!

209
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:16,610
What the…?

210
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:18,821
Did she steal my flash drive?!

211
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:21,490
That's why it was missing!

212
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:22,867
Chief!

213
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,410
We have to sue her!

214
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:27,246
We don't have enough proof!

215
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:29,123
Abi stealing it wasn't caught on cam.

216
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:32,543
But she triggered the fire alarm, right?

217
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:33,627
And you know what?

218
00:12:34,336 --> 00:12:36,881
I think she didn't just steal LoveFeast.

219
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:38,174
What else did she steal?

220
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:40,009
My shoes.

221
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,552
[CHARM] Shoes?

222
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:45,181
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:47,725
[MORRIE] So, this is the common area.

224
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:49,560
That's the pantry.

225
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:51,562
- Uh…
- [TELEPHONE RINGING]

226
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:54,773
Complete your requirements,
and I'll send you a list.

227
00:12:57,735 --> 00:13:00,613
[CHUCKLING, INHALES SHARPLY]

228
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:01,906
[SIGHS]

229
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:05,367
[CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

230
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:06,368
Oh!

231
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:07,953
I'm sorry.

232
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,873
I'm…
[SNIFFLES]

233
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,542
I'm just happy I finally have a job.

234
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,127
These are tears of joy.

235
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:17,171
- [ABI SNIFFLES]
- Okay.

236
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:21,467
Why is it called Pebblng?

237
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,219
You don't know why?

238
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:25,554
I'll do my research.

239
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:26,680
No, let me.

240
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,558
Pebblng a dating trend
inspired by penguins.

241
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:32,770
It's lovers giving each other
tokens of affection.

242
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:35,147
Like pebbles. Do you get it?

243
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,732
Absolutely.

244
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:38,192
I knew what it meant.

245
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:39,652
I thought there was a more…

246
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:42,988
you know, deeper meaning to it.

247
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:45,574
Anyway, standard requirements.

248
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,660
NDA. Background check.

249
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,787
No posting. No leaking.

250
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,705
What you see here stays here.

251
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,457
- Okay?
- Mm-hmm.

252
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,000
Anyway, I'll leave you to it.

253
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:57,336
- I'll be right here.
- All right, thank you.

254
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:01,757
[SIGHS]

255
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:05,177
[RAIN] Robbie?

256
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,054
- [ROBBIE] Yeah?
- Bill out for table five.

257
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:09,014
- [ROBBIE] Got it. Hold on.
- [PLATES CLATTERING]

258
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:14,186
I remember seeing Abi when I got home.

259
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:16,272
Ms. Billy!

260
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:17,439
- [DOOR SLAMS]
- [ABI] <i>Hello!</i>

261
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:18,440
Abi!

262
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:21,610
I went to the center earlier.

263
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:24,864
What for?

264
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:28,284
She kept bugging Auntie Pres.

265
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:30,077
She insisted on wanting to thank me.

266
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,829
And then the next day,

267
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:34,123
I lost my house keys.

268
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,918
I immediately had our lock changed.

269
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:41,297
<i>Auntie, did you see</i>
<i>my keys here last night?</i>

270
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,966
My shoes also went missing.

271
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:46,552
<i>Auntie, have you seen my red shoes?</i>

272
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:48,804
<i>The pair I wore</i>
<i>to the LoveList anniversary party.</i>

273
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:52,057
She was wearing
the exact shoes in Pebblng.

274
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,225
Dude.

275
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:55,185
That's creepy.

276
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:58,314
But there's no way to tell
if those were really mine.

277
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,608
I doubt it, though. It's the same pair.

278
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,111
Am I being petty for making
an issue out of my shoes?

279
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:05,362
Not really.

280
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,324
I'm more worried about you.

281
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,910
If she really did steal those
from your house…

282
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,455
then Abi is dangerous, dude.

283
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:17,583
I didn't know she was that bad.

284
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:19,126
We already lost an investor,

285
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:21,670
and we're also being accused of copying.

286
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,964
Okay, so Abi

287
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,258
planned all of this.

288
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:29,553
She pretended to be your friend

289
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,263
to have access to you.

290
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:32,640
To get info?

291
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:36,852
Maybe Camille sent her.

292
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,355
Like a mole. A spy.

293
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:42,399
Anyway.

294
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,361
Don't worry about Caloy.

295
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:47,613
I told you.

296
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:49,698
I can handle him.

297
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,867
I'm not done with Abi.

298
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:55,579
I just need a favor, please, dude.

299
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:58,582
Anything.

300
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:02,836
Boss.

301
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:04,672
That's a lot.

302
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:11,887
Still looking into Abi?

303
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:16,517
Billy went through a lot because of her.

304
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,018
She'll get through it.

305
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:19,561
Of course, 'cause you're there for her.

306
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:20,980
Same for her.

307
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,648
She's always there for me too.

308
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:24,191
Right.

309
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:28,612
No matter what bad luck comes your way,

310
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:29,822
you're both lucky.

311
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:31,740
Lucky in what sense?

312
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,742
You both have each other.

313
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:35,619
Ride or die, right?

314
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,330
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

315
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:46,463
Girls, I'm so sorry.
I know it's the weekend.

316
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:48,924
But we need to have a meeting tomorrow.

317
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:51,427
Oh.

318
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,721
What time?

319
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:54,972
[BILLY] <i>10:00 a.m.</i>

320
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:58,142
<i>We need to do some damage control.</i>

321
00:16:58,225 --> 00:17:01,061
<i>You already know what happened</i>
<i>with Ms. Lindsay.</i>

322
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:04,023
<i>We can't afford to lose</i>
<i>our other investors.</i>

323
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,442
Ah, okay.

324
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:10,237
<i>We need to come up with</i>
<i>a better plan than LoveFeast.</i>

325
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,655
So what now?

326
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,282
<i>We're moving on from LoveFeast?</i>

327
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:16,326
<i>We shouldn't just let that Abi</i>
<i>get away with it, right?</i>

328
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,078
<i>Chief, will you really let it slide?</i>

329
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,413
<i>Of course not.</i>

330
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:23,000
<i>Let's discuss our next move tomorrow.</i>

331
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,127
<i>All right. See you tomorrow.</i>

332
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:26,879
<i>Okay. Thanks, chief.</i>

333
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,338
<i>Okay. Bye.</i>

334
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:35,679
HOW WE WENT SILENT
BY BAYANI ROBLES

335
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,264
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

336
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,974
[YANI] Okay!

337
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,934
Last two, love!

338
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:41,977
Oh, okay.

339
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:45,981
I told you I could
bring them to the gallery.

340
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:48,817
It's okay, love. I'll go with you.

341
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:50,527
- [THUDS]
- I can handle it.

342
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,404
Look at you.

343
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:54,865
I know you're tired.

344
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:56,533
Not really.

345
00:17:57,159 --> 00:18:00,496
You know what?
Let's just meet at 10:00 a.m.

346
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:03,373
I'll be there by eight
because of how excited I am.

347
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,793
And it's been so long
since I've had my own exhibit.

348
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:07,503
But

349
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:09,630
I can feel it in my bones

350
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,841
that this will be my best series yet.

351
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,593
That's why I'm sure

352
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,929
that we'll make a lot of sales.

353
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:19,181
It's because I'm with my lucky charm!

354
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:20,557
[SMOOCHES, HUFFS]

355
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:22,518
And, of course,

356
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:26,730
this will surely be added
to our wedding budget.

357
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,067
- Right?
- Mm-hmm. [CHUCKLES]

358
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:34,738
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

359
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:37,533
I tried applying to Jordan's bar

360
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:39,118
to scope things out quickly.

361
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:40,869
But I got pissed off.

362
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:42,371
C'mon, Caloy.

363
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:45,082
- What did you expect?
- He kept talking about me!

364
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:48,001
I thought I already fooled him
during the hearing.

365
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,753
Turns out, he's still set
on putting me in jail.

366
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,964
Ah, they're really best friends.

367
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:53,966
Billy said the same thing.

368
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:56,093
"You better meet with your lawyers."

369
00:18:56,176 --> 00:18:58,595
Fine. She can do her worst.

370
00:18:58,679 --> 00:19:00,848
She has no idea that I can do worse.

371
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,307
[CHUCKLES]

372
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:05,394
What are we going to do, 'Bi? [SIGHS]

373
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:07,938
This.

374
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:10,440
What's in that?

375
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:11,608
A lot of things.

376
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:16,029
Even the list of investors is in here.

377
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:23,203
Billy said I was a thief.

378
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:24,371
[SCOFFS]

379
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:26,790
But she's the original thief herself!

380
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:30,961
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

381
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,088
- You're just the same.
- You're right!

382
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,756
We'll play then.

383
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,425
We'll play a game of tag.

384
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,136
- You're so bold.
- Go home!

385
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:42,097
Don't I get a cup of coffee?
I'll just use the bathroom.

386
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,390
- Stop!
- I need to pee.

387
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:45,309
You need to go home.

388
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:47,769
You're so stubborn, Caloy.

389
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:50,606
I've told you so many times
that we shouldn't meet.

390
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:51,773
But you won't listen!

391
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:54,359
Starting today, we really shouldn't meet!

392
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:56,778
I can't do that.

393
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:59,031
You know I can't leave you alone.

394
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:00,407
- Abi…
- You're such a flirt!

395
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:02,784
We're partners, right?
We should stick together.

396
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:06,413
C'mon, you don't need to play hard to get.

397
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:07,831
Fine.

398
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:09,041
I'll do anything.

399
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:12,127
I'll apologize to Jordan
even if I don't want to.

400
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,170
For you.

401
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:15,839
Do you really think he'll trust you?

402
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,091
I'll find a way!

403
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:20,427
I've been doing everything
for you, haven't I?

404
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:23,013
I'll do anything for you. C'mon!

405
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,849
You even look beautiful today.

406
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,684
- C'mon--
- Let go of her!

407
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:29,561
- Let go!
- Go home. Now.

408
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:32,522
Caloy, go home. Now!

409
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:41,156
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:45,452
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

411
00:20:48,205 --> 00:20:50,374
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

412
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:52,209
[NOTIFICATION CHIMES]

413
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,880
[JORDAN] <i>Don't worry, dude…</i>

414
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,675
<i>Abi won't get away with this.</i>

415
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:05,180
[BILLY] <i>She really won't, dude.</i>

416
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:07,182
<i>Thanks.</i>

417
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:14,022
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

418
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:22,447
You're bringing men here?

419
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:24,157
You're such a flirt!

420
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,243
That's your boyfriend!

421
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:28,578
Will you get fooled by a man too?

422
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,415
Didn't you learn from
your father's mistakes?

423
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:33,625
You'll turn out just like him!

424
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:35,627
He'll eventually leave you too!

425
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:37,170
What?

426
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:39,047
You're so…

427
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:41,174
You might end up leaving me!

428
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:43,093
He's not my boyfriend.

429
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:46,305
[MARIELA] That's exactly what
your father said to me.

430
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:49,057
He always denied it when I asked,

431
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:51,018
but the truth is, he was cheating on me!

432
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:53,061
You are all cheaters! Cheaters!

433
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:54,896
I am not like him!

434
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:59,026
I am not like my father!

435
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:00,861
Do you understand?

436
00:22:04,489 --> 00:22:06,033
And, Ma,

437
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:08,410
when did I ever leave you?

438
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:11,330
I never left you, haven't I?

439
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:15,834
I'm not dating around. I'm working!

440
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:18,754
I've got a new job.
Didn't I tell you about it this morning?

441
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:21,965
I'll be earning more.

442
00:22:22,049 --> 00:22:23,925
I'm doing this for us!

443
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:26,970
I want you to be proud of me.

444
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:30,057
Just like how proud you are of Abi!

445
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:32,976
- Where are you working?
- You don't need to know.

446
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,478
All I know is…

447
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:38,315
All I know is that our lives
will be better again.

448
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:39,733
[SIGHS]

449
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:45,530
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

450
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:48,700
- Billy.
- Aunt Pres.

451
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:52,412
- Here are the files you asked for on Abi.
- Thank you.

452
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:57,375
Is this the only record
she has in Angels of Grace?

453
00:22:57,459 --> 00:22:59,878
Yes. Just that.

454
00:23:00,837 --> 00:23:02,672
She wrote a different address
on her resumé

455
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:04,591
when she applied to LoveList.

456
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:07,928
She's giving fake addresses.

457
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:11,098
Could she also be lying about her mother?

458
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:15,018
I'll find something I can use
against this woman.

459
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:20,148
[PRECIOUS] <i>Billy,</i>
<i>if your suspicions are right,</i>

460
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,609
<i>maybe you should stay away from her.</i>

461
00:23:22,692 --> 00:23:25,695
<i>She's dangerous, Billy.</i>

462
00:23:26,488 --> 00:23:29,616
[BILLY] <i>If we let it slide,</i>
<i>then she'll do it again.</i>

463
00:23:29,699 --> 00:23:35,872
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:23:35,956 --> 00:23:40,085
I taught Oliver to fight back
when he was being wronged.

465
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:42,170
Lead by example, Aunt Pres.

466
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,548
But this is a different issue!

467
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:46,508
That's the thing. This is worse!

468
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,052
That's why she should pay for it.

469
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:51,096
Are you going to get even?

470
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:53,431
I'm not getting even, Aunt Pres.

471
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:56,184
It's collecting a debt.

472
00:23:57,227 --> 00:24:00,105
We lost so much
when she stole that project.

473
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:04,526
She even went inside our house!

474
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:06,111
We're not sure about that.

475
00:24:06,194 --> 00:24:09,197
But what if she was the one who went in?

476
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:13,201
You and Oliver could've gotten hurt!

477
00:24:13,285 --> 00:24:15,787
I won't let that slide.

478
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,916
She messed with the wrong person.

479
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:27,007
[TENSE MUSIC BUILDS, THEN FADES]

480
00:24:29,134 --> 00:24:30,969
<i>- Precious?</i>
<i>- Brandon?</i>

481
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,596
[BRANDON]
<i>What a coincidence!</i>

482
00:24:32,679 --> 00:24:34,055
[OLIVER]
<i>It was a giddy smile.</i>

483
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:37,267
- [BILLY] <i>Who is this man you're with?</i>
- [OLIVER] <i>That's Sir Eric.</i>

484
00:24:37,350 --> 00:24:40,729
[BILLY] <i>I remember this.</i>
<i>She said she owns an internet cafe.</i>

485
00:24:40,812 --> 00:24:42,147
<i>Where are you taking</i>
<i>my computers?!</i>

486
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:43,940
[CHARM] <i>How did you get</i>
<i>our files on LoveFeast?</i>

487
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:45,233
Let go of her!

488
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:46,735
[ABI] <i>Find that computer, okay?</i>

489
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,778
<i>Every single picture and video</i>
<i>on it has to be deleted!</i>

490
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:49,988
[JORDAN] <i>Where are you going?!</i>

491
00:24:50,071 --> 00:24:53,200
- [BOTH GRUNTING]
- [CALOY] Come on, hit me!

492
00:24:53,283 --> 00:24:55,952
<i>- How can I support you today?</i>
<i>- I'm Melissa.</i>

493
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:58,955
<i>I'm having second thoughts</i>
<i>about my wedding.</i>

494
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:00,457
<i>My dad doesn't approve of him.</i>

495
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:01,541
[JORDAN] <i>You need this.</i>

496
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:02,667
<i>You make it look so easy.</i>

497
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,920
<i>Being strong. Composed.</i>

498
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:06,129
<i>I could say the same to you.</i>

499
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:08,798
<i>Oh, very good!</i>

500
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:10,592
<i>- What's this?</i>
<i>- A friendship song.</i>

501
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:15,555
- [SINGING]<i> ♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>
- [GUITAR STRUMMING]

502
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:21,228
<i>♪ Let's just dance to the beat</i>
<i>Of our hearts ♪</i>

503
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:24,397
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

504
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:29,361
<i>♪ When you're crying ♪</i>
